    "body": "**Real-control check passed.** Contributor's Tormach 770MX, PathPilot v2.14.4, 2026-11-09. Build e2291de8, a top-face Z touch with T99 (tool length 5.2908, inch).\n- **Posted file:** the program posted from the GUI is byte-identical to the kit's. `(DEBUG, PROBE Z ERROR #190)` sits after the `o901` tolerance block and before `G10 L20 P1 Z[#5422-#190]`.\n- **Status window, two runs:** `PROBE Z ERROR -0.000276`, then `PROBE Z ERROR 0.000181` on the re-run (the second touches the offset the first one wrote). Both ran to the last line (33) with no stop: DEBUG is non-stopping, as the LinuxCNC reference says.\n- **Spindle:** stayed at 0 rpm throughout.\n- **Known and tracked elsewhere:** the non-blocking \"stock sim did not judge this program\" note on a probe-only program is #592; the rapid approach is fixed by #579/#570, which isn't in this build.\n\nFlagged ready.",
